<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sans-Souci Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1810">1810</a>–<a href="/years/1813">1813</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sans-Souci was the royal palace of Henri I, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a>, built at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milot">Milot</a> between 1810 and 1813. It was the seat of his court, with gardens, a chapel and government buildings, and Christophe shot himself there in October 1820. Ruined by the earthquake of 1842, it forms part of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> with the nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/citadelle-laferriere">Citadelle Laferrière</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sans-souci-palace.jpg" alt="Sans-Souci Palace" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iconem · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palais_du_sans-soucis.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
